metadata/_sms_note = "Pass 153k: KING BOO'S ROOM -- the casino boss room's WALL and CEILING from the game's own files (boss_wall.bmd, map.col, map.bmd): a 24-sided drum 33 m across, 54 m tall, painted with the stars-on-purple and the three drifting coloured spots (the game's three texture animations at once), closed by the marble ring and blue cap ceiling 47 m over the table. It BUILDS ITSELF when the scene opens (in the editor too), so the file holds nothing to see: the knobs are in the inspector. KingBooArena.tscn carries one as its BossWall child at the arena's own point; on its own, drop it where the table's node is -- it sits TableLiftUnits (500 u = 6.7 m) under that point, where the game stands it against its lifted discs. The outer disc's rim pokes 0.8 m into the wall: Mario cannot fall off the table any more. CeilingOn off opens the room to the sky; RoomCastsShadows on makes a dark indoor room (off: the sun lights the table as before); Brightness, SpotStrength and SpotSpeed tune the look (1 = the game's); WallRadiusUnits and the heights re-shape the drum."
